{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Laravel Performance Optimizer",
  "description": "Finds and fixes performance bottlenecks (N+1s, indexes, caching, eager loading) with concrete, low-risk optimizations.",
  "version": "2.0",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "app/**/*.php",
      "routes/**/*.php",
      "config/**/*.php",
      "database/**/*.php"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "LARAVEL PERFORMANCE OPTIMIZATION\n\nCONTEXT: Code was modified. Analyze and optimize performance bottlenecks.\n\nPROJECT STACK: Laravel 12, Filament v4, multi-tenant architecture with query scopes.\n\nOPTIMIZATION AREAS:\n\n**Database Performance:**\n- N+1 query detection and eager loading solutions\n- Query optimization with select() trimming\n- Index recommendations (foreign keys, slugs, timestamps)\n- Pagination and query scope reuse\n\n**Caching Strategy:**\n- Config/route/view cache opportunities\n- Query result caching where safe\n- Memoization of expensive computations\n- Queue offloading for heavy operations\n\n**Code Efficiency:**\n- Loop optimization and redundant query elimination\n- Collection usage for data transformations\n- Livewire render performance (keep lightweight)\n- Blade template optimization\n\n**Frontend Performance:**\n- Debounce/throttle for user interactions\n- Asset optimization considerations\n- Alpine.js performance patterns\n\nOUTPUT:\n1) **Performance Findings** by severity with file/line references\n2) **Optimization Solutions** with before/after code examples\n3) **Expected Impact** (query reduction, latency improvements)\n4) **Implementation Plan** with rollback strategies\n5) **Monitoring Recommendations** for validation\n\nMaintain behavior compatibility and respect existing policies/validation."
  },
  "shortName": "laravel-performance-optimizer"
}
